{"type":"message","id":"bed80609","parentId":"e96fa890","timestamp":"2026-03-31T17:19:45.610Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_HlQTJjZuPHUyfhBF65dV1D9Q|fc_05d0a16eaf1e343f0169cc023104c48191a2b0100fb97f4d42","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/TOOLS.md:22:- **Use for:** running the integrated kidney pipeline when an image should be uploaded and passed through the Kidney Cancer Detection model, the Image Analyzer component, and the downstream X-AI component.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/TOOLS.md:24:- **Meaning:** Produces a preliminary pipeline result structure; for quick summaries, prioritize these wanted outputs when present: the kidney cancer class, the kidney cancer confidence, the Image Analyzer prediction, and all available `cam_...` fields from the Image Analyzer output, especially the full `cam_metrics` set and `cam_explanation`.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/TOOLS.md:25:- **Presentation rule:** When reporting results to the user, do not default to low-level JSON labels. Present them in a cleaner summary with readable labels such as `Kidney cancer class`, `Confidence`, `Image Analyzer prediction`, `CAM coverage`, `CAM center ratio`, `CAM left-right asymmetry`, `CAM top-bottom asymmetry`, and `CAM explanation`.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/TOOLS.md:30:## skin-cancer-pipeline\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/TOOLS.md:31:- **Role:** Execute the fixed skin cancer detection pipeline starting from a skin image file.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/TOOLS.md:32:- **Use for:** running the integrated skin pipeline when an image should be uploaded and passed through the Skin Cancer Detection model, the Image Analyzer component, and the downstream X-AI component.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/TOOLS.md:34:- **Meaning:** Produces a preliminary pipeline result structure; for quick summaries, prioritize these wanted outputs when present: the skin cancer class, the skin cancer confidence, the Image Analy